-- title:
--   Ring-level Vélu formulas and naturality of Tate toric points
-- statement:
--   Over an arbitrary commutative ring $A$ with a Weierstrass curve $W$, the module defines division-free versions of Vélu's coordinate formulas, obtained from the field-level ones by replacing each quotient by `Ring.inverse`. For a finite set $S \subseteq A \times A$ of points, `veluXR W S x` is $x + \sum_{Q \in S} \bigl(t_Q\,\mathrm{inv}(x - Q_1) + u_Q\,\mathrm{inv}(x - Q_1)^2\bigr)$ and `veluYR W S x y` is $y$ minus $\sum_{Q \in S}\bigl(u_Q(2y + a_1x + a_3)\,\mathrm{inv}(x-Q_1)^3 + t_Q(a_1(x-Q_1) + y - Q_2)\,\mathrm{inv}(x-Q_1)^2 + (a_1u_Q - g_{x,Q}g_{y,Q})\,\mathrm{inv}(x-Q_1)^2\bigr)$, where $g_x = 3x^2 + 2a_2x + a_4 - a_1y$, $g_y = -(2y + a_1x + a_3)$, $t = 2g_x - a_1g_y$, $u = g_y^2$ are the quantities `veluGx`, `veluGy`, `veluT`, `veluU`. Over a field these agree with [`WeierstrassCurve.veluX`](../def/WeierstrassCurve_VeluQuotientMap.html#L47) and [`WeierstrassCurve.veluY`](../def/WeierstrassCurve_VeluPointMap.html#L51). Similarly `vcXInvR C x` $= (u^{-1})^2(x - r)$ and `vcYInvR C x y` $= (u^{-1})^3(y - t - s(x-r))$ invert a change of variables $C = (u,r,s,t)$ over a commutative ring, agreeing over a field with [`WeierstrassCurve.Affine.vcXInv`](../def/WeierstrassCurve_VariableChangePointEquiv.html#L18) and `vcYInv`. Finally `toricXCoeff p c m` names the coefficient function whose associated power series gives the first coordinate of the toric point `tateToricPoint A p c`: it is $c\,\mathrm{inv}(1-c)^2$ for $m = 0$ and otherwise $\sum_{d \mid m,\ p \mid d} (m/d)\bigl(c^{m/d} + c^{-m/d}\bigr) - 2\,[p \mid m]\sum_{e \mid m/p} e$.
--
--   The accompanying lemmas record naturality and unit criteria. Along a ring homomorphism $f \colon A \to B$ the coefficientwise map $A((q)) \to B((q))$ commutes with `HahnSeries.ofPowerSeries`, with constants, with `laurentOfInt`, carries the Tate curve over $A((q))$ to that over $B((q))$, and carries `tateToricPoint A p c` to `tateToricPoint B p (f c)` provided $1 - c$ is a unit; $f$ commutes with `Ring.inverse` at units, with the Vélu quantities, with `vcXInvR`/`vcYInvR`, and with `veluXR`/`veluYR` when $\mathrm{Prod.map}\,f\,f$ is injective on $S$ and all $x - Q_1$ are units. A power series with unit constant term gives a unit of $A((q))$; combined with the polynomial identity $c w_c^2 - d w_d^2 = w_c^2 w_d^2 (c-d)(1 - cd)$ for $w_c(1-c) = w_d(1-d) = 1$, this shows that the difference of the first coordinates of `tateToricPoint A p c` and `tateToricPoint A p d` is a unit whenever $1 - c$, $1 - d$, $c - d$ and $1 - cd$ are units.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib supplies `WeierstrassCurve`, `VariableChange`, Hahn and Laurent series and `Ring.inverse`; the Vélu coordinate maps `veluX`/`veluY`, the variable-change inverses `vcXInv`/`vcYInv`, the Tate curve over $A((q))$ and its toric points are project notions. The definitions here are the `Ring.inverse` analogues of those field-level formulas over an arbitrary commutative ring.
--
--   **Where it is used.** These ring-level formulas and their compatibility with base change supply the computation of the quotient of the Tate curve by the subgroup generated by a toric point over a cyclotomic base ring, and its specialisation to any field containing a primitive root of unity, which is how the relation between $j(E_q)$ and $j(q^d)$ is transferred from characteristic zero in the modular-curve part of the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_ModularCurve_TateVeluRing.lean

